FILE narrow-d436/audit-v1-codex.md
     1	The passage is **not sound**: it turns “two sides of one bet” into a rule that always chooses the whole figure. That choice is not in D436, and it can settle cases that D631 and D635 leave open.
     2	
     3	For example, the passage would choose total passenger numbers over whether planes stay full. But D436 also gives the opposite orientation: demand is the figure, while capacity keeping pace is the side left as context. This is a read-only assessment of the text and supplied cases; no model was called.
     4	
     5	1. **Clause by clause**
     6	
     7	| Inserted clause | Verdict | Reason and collision |
     8	|---|---|---|
     9	| “a figure together with a part of that same figure … [is] one bet seen from two sides” | **Keeps wider** | [D436](</Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:4847>) recognizes the AI-chip share beside the chip total as one bet. It does not say every whole-and-part pair is necessarily one bet. |
    10	| “or with a condition on it” | **Keeps wider** | D436 identifies particular second sides; it does not make every condition on every figure a second side of the same bet. A condition can itself be a separately tracked outcome. |
    11	| “not several things with none the main one” | **Contradicts / keeps wider** | This declares a main part whenever the broad whole-and-part or figure-and-condition pattern matches. [D397](</Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:4326>) says a topic with no main part gets no question; [D631](</Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:8527>) and [D635](</Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:8618>) leave the choice open when several parts are named. It collides with the decline case in [system line 6](</Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/reflection-8/narrow-d436/frozen-system.txt:6>) and the same case in the [schema’s `no_ladder` description](</Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/candidate-schema.json:19>). |
    12	| “ask the figure, and list the part or the condition in `not_judged`” | **No source for the selection rule; contradicts D436’s demand example** | Listing the unjudged side is consistent with D436 and D397. Automatically choosing the whole figure is not. It also collides with “Judge the one the topic’s outcome names as what is tracked” in [system line 5](</Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/reflection-8/narrow-d436/frozen-system.txt:5>) and the [closing check](</Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/candidate-closing.txt:1>) when the outcome names several without selecting the whole. |
    13	| The four examples | **Keep wider; one reverses D436’s orientation** | Each teaches the same automatic choice. The airline example selects passenger count over capacity utilization, whereas D436’s capacity-and-demand example makes demand the figure and capacity keeping pace the side. See item 5. |
    14	| “Two separate figures, or one figure for two years, are still several things” | **No source as a general rule; ambiguous against D436** | The request already requires one figure for a named period. Two equally tracked annual figures can support a decline. But D436’s demand and capacity example can contain two separate figures as sides of one bet, and a previous year can be a comparison rather than another tracked question. See item 6. |
