    57	The concern remains that the passage decides **other** multi-part outcomes by surface shape. These six do not demonstrate that particular failure.
    58	
    59	### 5. Examples
    60	
    61	The insertion contains **three explicit examples**, not four. The general sentence also describes three shapes but is a rule, not a fourth worked example.
    62	
    63	- **Bank lending and commercial share:** mirrors the total-and-component structure of **acc/clean-9**. It does not use its company, product or numbers.
    64	- **Retail sales and shelves running short:** mirrors the shipments-and-shortage structure of **acc/clean-8**, though sales and shelf availability are not necessarily the same bet merely because they appear together.
    65	- **Utility demand and capacity keeping pace:** closely mirrors **acc/clean-10**, which asks NAND demand and whether capacity additions keep pace. Its orientation agrees with D436: demand is judged and capacity is the side.
    66	
    67	Thus, the examples are from other industries and do not copy the test articles’ names or figures, but they **mirror test-topic structures**, especially the utility example. The wording does not read identically across industries: lending, shelves and generating capacity are industry-specific illustrations. Their relationships can be translated across industries, but the reader still has to decide whether each pair represents one bet; the passage currently assumes it does.
    68	
