    47	## 4. D631’s six boundary cases
    48	
    49	On the supplied wording, **none is clearly decided by the new passage**. That is a finding about these six inputs, not proof that the general wording cannot decide another unresolved case.
    50	
    51	| Boundary case | Effect |
    52	|---|---|
    53	| Optical-switch shipments | Several checkpoints and a full-year volume; neither a part/share, shortage nor capacity-versus-demand pair. No new selection. |
    54	| Chip sales into China | Two authorities’ decisions and resulting revenue; not one of the three shapes. No new selection. |
    55	| Acquisition | Agreement, closing, consideration and conditions; not one of the three shapes. No new selection. |
    56	| Investment commitments | Remaining balance, cash funded and changes in commitments. The edit does not expressly say that a stock balance and a cash flow are a total and its share. A model could stretch the example to choose a balance, but the wording does not clearly require it. |
    57	| Memory prices | Contract prices, producers’ selling prices and margins are different measures, not a total and its share. No new selection. |
    58	| Chip export licence | Licence status and resumed revenue are distinct events/measures. No new selection. |
    59	
    60	The general risk remains: “tracks a figure” plus “ask the figure” can select a figure in an unresolved total-and-component outcome, even though none of these six unambiguously triggers it.
    61	
    62	## 5. Examples
    63	
    64	The passage contains **three written examples**, not four: bank lending, retailer sales and utility demand. It also names three abstract shapes.
    65	
    66	- **Mirroring the 44 test topics:** Yes, structurally. The bank example mirrors **acc/clean-9**’s total plus component; the retailer example mirrors **acc/clean-8**’s shipment/supply plus shortage; and the utility example mirrors **acc/clean-10**’s demand plus capacity keeping pace. The examples do not copy those topics’ named companies, products or numbers. Nevertheless, §6 says no example is taken from a test article and requires examples that teach a general rule; substituting industries does not erase the close structural mirroring. [Test topics](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/stage_a/cases.json)
    67	- **Across industries:** The relationships can be understood in banking, drugs, retail and chips, but the wording itself names three specific industries rather than presenting portable examples in each. The retailer example’s sales-versus-empty-shelves relationship is also less precise: sales can be constrained by availability, while shortage depends on demand as well.
    68	- **Orientation:** The examples consistently choose **total lending**, **sales**, and **demand**, respectively. The third agrees with D436: demand is the figure and capacity keeping pace is the side. This does not make capacity the main figure in the different u3/clean-10 target.
    69	
    70	## 6. Growth
    71	
    72	**No.** The recorded reason identifies a potentially missing instruction and says two audits found no obvious sentence to cut. That is a useful explanation, but it does not complete §6’s requirement to remove at least as much elsewhere when adding an instruction, or to report prompt tokens before and after. The token comparison is deferred to a paid send, so it has not yet been reported. The passage grows from **9,545 to 10,217 characters**, an increase of **672**. [AGENTS.md §6](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/AGENTS.md:194)
    73	
    74	NOT SOUND: Require the outcome to identify the figure as the main tracked part before applying the D436 examples; express shipment growth accurately, avoid test-topic mirrors, and make the required compensating cut and token comparison.     1	(The Claude-family blind auditor's report on version 3, received as its final message on 2026-11-17 and stored by Claude; condensed.)
     2	Verdict line: NOT SOUND: replace "a retailer's holiday sales" with a full-year figure, so no example asks a figure for part of a year that line 6 declines; also correct edit.json's "Alex's words" attribution.
     3	Otherwise: clauses a, b, c consistent with D436 (a keeps somewhat wider: a loose reading could invert a share-tracked outcome such as u3/clean-11; "also" guards it); the carve-out from line 6 is explicit; no_ladder's description does not repeat it (a tension, not a contradiction). Targets: acc/clean-8, acc/clean-9, pool-17 as D436 rules; u3/clean-10 by extension of clause b (capacity as the supply figure), the most interpretive. Controls: the passage fires on none of the eight on a careful reading; u2/clean-10 fragile (watch it). Boundary cases: none decided; investment commitments the only share-like wording, does not fire on a careful reading (keep as a control). Examples: none from the 44 (searched); structurally mirror acc/clean-9, -8, -10 one for one (inherent in carrying D436's shapes), so acc/clean-8 and -9 are fitted cases and only pool-17 and u3/clean-10 test generalisation. Attribution: D436's parenthetical is the recorder's Decided line; Alex's own words are "算一个题，第三处不改" in reply to an option with the HBM example only. Growth: the reason suffices for the content; the cut search and a $0 token count should be recorded; the passage repeats itself and could be trimmed.

codex
**DISAGREE: do not send v4 yet.** It makes an untested general choice about which question matters, and the test as implemented can pass without checking all the harms we agreed to check.

For example, an outcome can track both a bank’s total lending and its commercial-lending share. The passage says to ask the total whenever that shape appears. That may be right for a topic about the total; it may discard the central question when the topic is about the share. The word “tracks” does not resolve that distinction. [v4 passage](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/reflection-8/narrow-d436/edit.json:4)

1. **Is v4 fit for the paired test? No.** D436 supports the named examples and keeping a second side of the same bet as context. V4 goes further: it declares every matching total-and-share or supply-and-shortage shape to be one bet and selects the figure. The v3 Codex auditor identified that exact risk; v4 changes the growth-rate wording but does not resolve it. [D436](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:4847), [v3 Codex audit](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/reflection-8/narrow-d436/audit-v3-codex.md:9)

   I also would **not** require an explicit “main figure” label in every outcome: that could reproduce the refusal we are trying to address. The unresolved issue is how to express the *same bet* relationship without making the shape alone decide importance. Test that distinction at $0 with source-backed counterexamples, including a share-centred topic, before sending.

   The proposed `u3/clean-10` target needs separate treatment: it asks about **capacity additions and their timing**, whereas D436’s recorded third example is **demand with capacity keeping pace**. Do not count that target as a directly settled orientation without a source-backed determination. [Target](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/reflection-8/narrow-d436/audit-topics.json:15), [v3 audit](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/reflection-8/narrow-d436/audit-v3-codex.md:21)

2. **The cheaper reversible course is the $0 audit, not this send.** The paid test can measure behaviour on its cases; it cannot decide whether a broad rule is supported or safe on cases absent from the test. V4 is also a new version: the auditors’ verdicts were on v3, not this exact passage. Record both positions and have independent readers check v4’s changed wording, the share-centred counterexample, and the capacity target before deciding on a send.

   The size report is now complete: **+741 characters and +151 tokens**, with a written reason. The request still needs the required cut/merge search considered against that reason; the reported growth alone is not evidence that the passage works. [Edit record](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/reflection-8/narrow-d436/edit.json:19)

3. **The paired rule and implementation need correction before any send.**

   - **Require the source review to affect the verdict.** The code passes targets on the four hard-line marks alone. A question can clear those marks yet use an invented measure or an unsuitable deadline. Our agreed plan required every replacement to be reviewed against its source and material harm to stop progress; the current `score()` does not incorporate that review. [Scoring code](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/reflection-8/narrow-d436/paired_probe.py:197)
   - **Do not count a lost unchanged answer as an exercised refusal.** The code counts every status other than `ladder` toward the six, including an answer refused twice by code. Exercise should require an actual model decline of a source-confirmed target. Also report exercise by topic: six declines on only two topics do not demonstrate the other two failure shapes. [Scoring code](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/reflection-8/narrow-d436/paired_probe.py:208)
   - **Verify the eight controls against their full inputs and theme list.** The v3 audit could not establish every control from the supplied topic alone. A correct question should not be penalized merely because a control was presumed to require a refusal. [v3 audit](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/reflection-8/narrow-d436/audit-v3-codex.md:32)
   - **Correct the budget before launch.** The code sets **$2.70 per arm**, or **$5.40 total**, and estimates **$1.40 per arm**, or **$2.80 total**. Those differ from the proposed $3.20 combined cap and ~$2.10 estimate. With $1.49 and $0.17 already spent, the code’s full caps would exceed the approximately $6 discussed. [Caps](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/reflection-8/narrow-d436/paired_probe.py:39)

Keep the strict zero-fault target rule. Fix the candidate’s boundary and the test’s verdict and budget first; then the council can decide whether the exposed comparison is informative enough to send. **DISAGREE.**
